Package: rhodep-gpu-opencl
Version: 4
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: rhodep port
Depends: mesa-opencl-icd, clinfo
Description: OpenCL on the Adreno 619 via rusticl for Motorola rhodep
 Mesa's rusticl provides OpenCL on freedreno, but it ships disabled and only
 turns on when RUSTICL_ENABLE names the driver. Without it clinfo reports zero
 platforms and consumers see no GPU. This sets RUSTICL_ENABLE=freedreno
 system-wide so OpenCL consumers see FD619, and the GPU runs kernels correctly
 (verified with pyopencl).
 .
 Note: hashcat specifically fails with CL_INVALID_WORK_ITEM_SIZE on its own
 kernels even at local size 1, a hashcat<->rusticl/freedreno issue, not a
 configuration one - plain OpenCL kernels run fine. Other OpenCL loads work.
